  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Delivering life-saving assistance and protection to people fleeing Sudan and assist the most vulnerable South Sudan returnees through integrated protection action</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide protection, camp coordination and camp management (CCCM), and logistics assistance to vulnerable people seeking refuge in South Sudan from fighting in neighboring Sudan. This UNHCR project will monitor border activities, register refugees and returnees, identify and assist people with special needs, construct community shelters and facilitate transportation of refugees and asylum-seekers as well as of core relief items, among other activities. The project provides life-saving assistance to 11,500 people in the Protection sector, 11,500 people in the CCCM sector and 2,500 people in the Common Services -Logistics sector.</narrative>
  </description>
